Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:22:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe: Add the PS/2 mouse

SioBusDxe creates the COM ports and the PS/2 keyboard only, so
Ps2MouseDxe, which binds to a PNP0F03 or PNP0F13 device, never starts:
the TrackPoint and the touchpad of a laptop, on the auxiliary port of
the keyboard controller, do not work in the firmware.

Add a PS/2 mouse (PNP0F03). Ps2MouseDxe installs its simple pointer only
when a keyboard controller answers and a device acknowledges on its
auxiliary port (an absent mouse costs one 50 ms timeout), and the
keyboard driver leaves the bytes of the auxiliary port to it: it stops
reading when the status register flags them. Platforms without
Ps2MouseDxe are not affected.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe/SioService.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe/SioService.c b/OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe/SioService.c
index 66c5a08cf9..957b22c626 100644
--- a/OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe/SioService.c
+++ b/OvmfPkg/SioBusDxe/SioService.c
@@ -54,6 +54,17 @@ SIO_RESOURCES_IO  mPs2KeyboardDeviceResources = {
   { ACPI_END_TAG_DESCRIPTOR, 0             }
 };
 
+//
+// PS/2 Mouse, on the auxiliary port of the PS/2 keyboard controller
+//
+GLOBAL_REMOVE_IF_UNREFERENCED
+SIO_RESOURCES_IO  mPs2MouseDeviceResources = {
+  {
+    { ACPI_FIXED_LOCATION_IO_PORT_DESCRIPTOR }, 0x60, 5
+  },
+  { ACPI_END_TAG_DESCRIPTOR, 0             }
+};
+
 //
 // Table of SIO Controllers
 //
@@ -73,7 +84,12 @@ SIO_DEVICE_INFO  mDevicesInfo[] = {
     EISA_PNP_ID (0x303),
     0,
     { (ACPI_SMALL_RESOURCE_HEADER *)&mPs2KeyboardDeviceResources }
-  }   // PS/2 Keyboard Controller
+  },  // PS/2 Keyboard Controller
+  {
+    EISA_PNP_ID (0xF03),
+    0,
+    { (ACPI_SMALL_RESOURCE_HEADER *)&mPs2MouseDeviceResources    }
+  }   // PS/2 Mouse
 };
 
